0239: Draw the UI in the present pass instead of its own full-window pass

The present path used two render passes on the swap chain texture: the blit (or postfx chain) with
LoadOp::Clear, then a second pass with LoadOp::Load + Store that drew only the UI over the image the
first pass had just written. The second pass loaded and stored every pixel of the window for a few
thousand UI pixels (the FPS counter, notices, the F1 menu): 6.6 Mpix at 1680x988 points on a Retina
panel (3360x1976 pixels), 2.2-2.6 ms per frame with AURORA_GPU_PROFILE=1 on a base M1 (7-core GPU).
The UI goes into the present pass, after the blit/postfx and the RmlUi overlay: the profile's "ImGui"
zone is gone, its cost is inside "Present blit".

